Privacy Policy
Effective Date: May 8, 2026
Welcome to TropangAI. We respect your privacy and we want to be upfront about what data we collect, why we collect it, and how it's used. This Privacy Policy applies to anyone who uses TropangAI — no matter who you are.

1. What We Collect
Firebase Authentication
When you sign in with Google, we receive basic profile information including your:
Email address
Display name
Profile picture
This is used solely to identify your account and keep your data separate from other users. We do not access your Google account beyond what is needed to sign you in.
Firestore Database
We store the following data in our database to make the app work:
Conversations — the title and timestamp of your chat threads so you can find them later.
Messages — every message you send and every AI response within your conversations.
File Metadata — the filename, size, and upload date of documents you upload.
Document Content — the extracted text from your uploaded PDFs. This is what the AI reads to answer your questions (this is how RAG works).
Browser Local Storage
We save your theme preference (dark mode or light mode) locally in your browser. This never leaves your device and is not sent to our servers.

2. How We Use Your Data
We use your data only to provide and improve TropangAI. Specifically:
To authenticate your identity and keep your documents private from other users.
To let the AI answer questions based on your uploaded documents.
To save your conversation history so you can come back to it later.
To remember your display preferences.
We do not sell your data. We do not use your data for advertising. We do not share your data with third parties except as required to operate the service (e.g., Firebase/Google infrastructure).

3. Data Sharing
Your data is processed through the following third-party services:
Google Firebase — for authentication and database storage. Google's privacy policy applies to their services.
GROQ API — your document content and questions are sent to GROQ to generate AI responses. GROQ's privacy policy applies to their service.
Beyond these services, we do not share your personal data with anyone.

4. Data Security
Your documents and conversations are stored per-account and are not accessible by other users. We use Firebase's built-in security rules to enforce this. That said, no system is 100% secure — please do not upload documents containing highly sensitive information (like passwords, financial credentials, or government IDs).

5. Your Rights
You have the right to:
Access the data we store about you.
Delete your account and all associated data.
Stop using TropangAI at any time.
To request data deletion or ask questions about your data, please contact us.

6. Changes to This Policy
We may update this Privacy Policy from time to time. If we make significant changes, we'll do our best to let you know. Continued use of TropangAI after changes means you accept the updated policy.


